ype {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{\\pi }^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abd54eb7-1086-539a-8add-746e03dd04ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277021} :answer-field/id #uuid "c006b05b-e312-5e14-bc62-bb96f8a28156" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278066}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e406b09c-bfce-50a6-b8a5-dd556a32ecbf" :question/math-academy-id "q-159585" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy,$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(0,\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-xy) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(0,\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡0-\\pi  \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\pi -1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45268c40-f590-50a8-ba1a-21b858fce141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276088} {:answer/id #uuid "6951a819-e923-55cf-bd46-3c7b08d10b89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276422} 