& =6 (-1) (1)^{2}+(1) \\\\  & =-6+(1) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019ef7fd-1e40-5bfa-b396-c65b7986b509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560257} {:answer/id #uuid "879a6590-6d16-5057-9f9b-f643a19b8efc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560281} {:answer/id #uuid "da8bb81f-1925-585b-8a5a-bc3432ec5ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560289} {:answer/id #uuid "eda61f1e-52c0-529f-87ce-9712ea47c7f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560295} {:answer/id #uuid "f1342a2b-1459-59d2-89f7-1a0aff24bc4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "019ef7fd-1e40-5bfa-b396-c65b7986b509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560257} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cb4fff8-45ad-50c3-8b2e-9b437dd13890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560273}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2c0e388-7239-552d-8839-6c9035d1a779" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=3 y^{2} x^{2}+2 y x,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 y^{2} x^{2}+2 y x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 y^{2} x^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 y x) \\\\  & =3 x^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{2})+2 x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =3 x^{2}\\cdot (2 y)+2 x\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =6 y x^{2}+2 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & =6 (1) (1)^{2}+2 (1) \\\\  & =6+(2) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560297 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ea927af-1007-572a-922f-4aefb0c8767e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560264} {:answer/id #uuid "61615a5c-1c97-5ca0-97b9-f795b28e5c8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560274} {:answer/id #uuid "64686f40-7ee7-549c-8a01-588a18b5d8b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560276} {:answer/id #uuid "7176a7f5-da12-53cf-9ffd-85f92b2fb510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560279} {:answer/id #uuid "e1c4d2a1-1c92-5c12-9540-6b62a7ee553f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea927af-1007-572a-922f-4aefb0c8767e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560264} :answer-field/id #uuid "371473f6-d498-5af3-980f-2a37043ccdd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560268}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f71f04b5-8161-5a16-8003-15968bea5986" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=3 x^{2} y^{2}+x y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x^{2} y^{2}+x y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x^{2} y^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x y) \\\\  & =3 y^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2})+y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =3 y^{2}\\cdot (2 x)+y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =6 x y^{2}+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(-2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(-2,1)} & =6 (-2) (1)^{2}+(1) \\\\  & =-12+(1) \\\\  & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712881 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06308084-f04f-5090-a6f4-dd6060453a59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712871} {:answer/id #uuid "14e59890-4537-539d-b6fc-ff850eb4b3ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712875} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1bc1bf-d3ca-5ef6-95b7-232e988ce093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712878} {:answer/id #uuid "693711ce-f4b2-59ed-acf8-f6c94c65b436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712884} {:answer/id #uuid "ac899296-7aad-5d7e-a301-0ccc2faa4594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06308084-f04f-5090-a6f4-dd6060453a59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712871} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6510e5a-1b86-5bd8-87f9-467d5ff85b2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712891}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54f4d22d-a239-5fcb-afa5-eee103469884" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x^2y+y^3$, evaluate $f_x(2,3)$.\n\nTreat $y$ as a constant when differentiating with respect to $x$." :question/worked-solution "Hold $y$ fixed. The factor $y$ in $x^2y$ is constant, and the entire term $y^3$ is constant with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=y\\frac{d}{dx}(x^2)+\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(y^3)\\\\\n&=y(2x)+0\\\\\n&=2xy.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow substitute the coordinates into the derivative:\n\n$$\nf_x(2,3)=2\\cdot2\\cdot3=12.\n$$\n\nThe requested value is a derivative value, rather than the function value $f(2,3)=39$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a852a4-0a69-55ed-8493-76cf63e4cddf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712873} {:answer/id #uuid "3d34b0ad-a4d4-5ec4-83fe-9ce7625d8328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712879} {:answer/id #uuid "46717083-3ffb-584a-a9a0-063b0c06f24c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712880} {:answer/id #uuid "7f65060f-5112-5914-9f08-b8e78ec33a4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712885} {:answer/id #uuid "95637d02-e879-5b64-90ff-74a4a5945e62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46717083-3ffb-584a-a9a0-063b0c06f24c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712880} :answer-field/id #uuid "09829f4f-95be-53fa-a7c9-b1a5f8e86c0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712872}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "806fd5f6-6859-5b61-b789-17ba59235429" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y^2\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y}$, evaluate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(9,3)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, holding $x$ fixed. In particular, $\\sqrt{x}$ and $x$ are constant factors. Rewrite the reciprocal as a negative power:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(x,y)&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(y^2\\sqrt{x}+xy^{-1}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{x}(2y)+x(-y^{-2})\\\\\n&=2y\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{x}{y^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate both contributions at $(9,3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(9,3)&=2\\cdot3\\cdot\\sqrt{9}-\\frac{9}{3^2}\\\\\n&=18-1\\\\\n&=17.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712888 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "132fe52c-77a0-545d-8cf3-d20c12b04079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712874} {:answer/id #uuid "1f7da2fb-1a07-530a-b156-87159f2af2f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712876} {:answer/id #uuid "551c7c6e-6e0b-58c9-b3c9-5024b1b3d3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712882} {:answer/id #uuid "5553a4af-1906-5ebb-b828-38daa741b83d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712883} {:answer/id #uuid "ad471761-0632-55a5-8ee0-af5ff0a4025f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad471761-0632-55a5-8ee0-af5ff0a4025f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712890} :answer-field/id #uuid "239aa3a4-e9f0-5cc3-8909-af64520d468d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712877}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "957500c8-da71-5970-a3fc-26819b4da2c7" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=x\\sec y+x^4y$, evaluate $f_y\\left(\\sqrt{2},-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $x^4$ as constant factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(x,y)&=x\\frac{d}{dy}(\\sec y)+x^4\\frac{d}{dy}(y)\\\\\n&=x\\sec y\\tan y+x^4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the given point, the exact values are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sec\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=\\sqrt{2},\\\\\n\\tan\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)&=-1,\\\\\n(\\sqrt{2})^4&=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute these into the derivative and combine the two contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y\\left(\\sqrt{2},-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\n&=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot\\sqrt{2}\\cdot(-1)+4\\\\\n&=-2+4\\\\\n&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "220093e7-a461-5b2a-8682-00e542189f3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2 + e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713577} {:answer/id #uuid "362b31ee-223c-513c-9554-9413ca96e757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713584} {:answer/id #uuid "43cbf49e-792e-5eef-a89c-230e73d2cbfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713589} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2c5e96-d1b9-53be-b6e3-75e7debfc8ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713593} {:answer/id #uuid "be719cd8-1090-5075-a416-e2b99b116e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d2c5e96-d1b9-53be-b6e3-75e7debfc8ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713593} :answer-field/id #uuid "830b09d1-f6bd-52c8-a965-a029f25a15d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713595}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "099e0544-01a4-5351-9f4b-f28293480bcc" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=e^{x} \\ln{(y )}+2 y x^{5}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{x} \\ln{(y )}+2 y x^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(e^{x} \\ln{(y )})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 y x^{5}) \\\\  & =e^{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln{(y )})+2 x^{5}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y) \\\\  & =e^{x}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{y}\\right)+2 x^{5}\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =\\frac{e^{x}}{y}+2 x^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & =\\frac{e^{(1)}}{(1)}+2 (1)^{5} \\\\  & =2 + e\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713588 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13cb6587-709d-58d4-8c35-3c964c49fdd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 - \\frac{e^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713575} {:answer/id #uuid "27f1c4d3-2577-5e65-b829-cfc119e6361f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}}{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713581} {:answer/id #uuid "4796747b-9d78-50ce-a83f-648f226b3d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713590} {:answer/id #uuid "d148f018-b38a-55d6-8339-7dc6c05fb3f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713600} {:answer/id #uuid "f8066404-805d-5092-90a0-d52cc65aa766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}}{2} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f1c4d3-2577-5e65-b829-cfc119e6361f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}}{2} + 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713581} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a46d369-f891-5368-a7cf-81f7909c6d45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713587}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ec62fc4-7aca-5cde-bae7-34335042abde" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y^{4} \\ln{(x )}+\\sqrt{y} x$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(e^{2},1)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{4} \\ln{(x )}+\\sqrt{y} x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{4} \\ln{(x )})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{y} x) \\\\  & =\\ln{(x )}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{4})+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\ln{(x )}\\cdot (4 y^{3})+x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{y}}\\right) \\\\  & =4 y^{3} \\ln{(x )}+\\frac{x}{2 \\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(e^{2},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(e^{2},1)} & =4 (1)^{3} \\ln{(e^{2})}+\\frac{(e^{2})}{2 \\sqrt{(1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{e^{2}}{2} + 8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2357388b-1c0a-5418-8583-7690efc9203e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713578} {:answer/id #uuid "350cab05-11d6-5690-b2e1-999dd505e7b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713583} {:answer/id #uuid "397aa157-380f-5e68-a2e8-50e0c3f46dbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713586} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a28110-035a-5e87-80ab-5e6d8984abad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713597} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ac340a-9749-5ef5-8f72-aff73eb50f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a28110-035a-5e87-80ab-5e6d8984abad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713597} :answer-field/id #uuid "267809e4-876e-5a5a-8c1e-e415b4743636" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713579}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c9edc195-823a-5c2e-ac4b-ba7ca607ff90" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x}+\\frac{x}{y}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x}+x{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 y^{2} \\sqrt{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =4 \\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{2})+x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =4 \\sqrt{x}\\cdot (2 y)+x\\cdot (-{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =8 y \\sqrt{x}-x{y}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(1,1)} & =8 (1) \\sqrt{(1)}-(1){(1)}^{-2} \\\\  & =8-(1) \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a500e4e-9397-59ff-a942-fafcfbf25879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713574} {:answer/id #uuid "200d9ced-4a51-555c-8ee2-a3686764f729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713576} {:answer/id #uuid "38186fba-8a54-5694-bce9-ce3720e1c6db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713585} {:answer/id #uuid "56cbea0d-8e2d-5601-beb9-8c51ab2fb1c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713592} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b1296a-1e37-5913-be4e-0b6764a72da1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0b1296a-1e37-5913-be4e-0b6764a72da1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713596} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffef58a3-ae4e-5856-9643-45462a95e8f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713606}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df51131e-8df4-541c-9fa4-ddeb842a43b4" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y \\sqrt{x}-3 \\sqrt{y} x$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ at the point $(4,4)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y \\sqrt{x}-3 \\sqrt{y} x) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y \\sqrt{x})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 \\sqrt{y} x) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)-3 x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (1)-3 x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{y}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{3 x}{2 \\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(4,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(4,4)} & =\\sqrt{(4)}-\\frac{3 (4)}{2 \\sqrt{(4)}} \\\\  & =2-(3) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186713607 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26fdd424-f0d6-5c5a-875e-ec5e83e5cc69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} + \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713580} {:answer/id #uuid "286eb541-0a80-5a89-abdf-e55cf252483e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713582} {:answer/id #uuid "490d67da-3cf7-5576-83a1-7a72b81fe931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713591} {:answer/id #uuid "5e33bb59-29f4-5885-abf1-74c34d98c754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - 2 \\ln{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713594} {:answer/id #uuid "ee36c59a-85cb-516f-836c-3411fbc55ae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{6}{\\pi} + \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "490d67da-3cf7-5576-83a1-7a72b81fe931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - \\frac{6}{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713591} :answer-field/id #uuid "e93aa025-9f60-584a-82b4-f55ed4aa2d66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186713603}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fff0c50f-8039-5b75-8c50-72eec2dabcc5" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=2 \\ln{(x )} \\cos{(y )}-3 y \\sin{(x )}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}$ at the point $\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 \\ln{(x )} \\cos{(y )}-3 y \\sin{(x )}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 \\ln{(x )} \\cos{(y )})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 y \\sin{(x )}) \\\\  & =2 \\cos{(y )}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln{(x )})-3 y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sin{(x )}) \\\\  & =2 \\cos{(y )}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)-3 y\\cdot (\\cos{(x )}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\cos{(y )}}{x}-3 y \\cos{(x )}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi\\right):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\pi\\right)} & =\\frac{2 \\cos{(\\pi)}}{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}-3 (\\pi) \\cos{\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)} \\\\  & =- \\frac{6}{\\pi}-\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} - \\frac{6}{\\pi}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Partial Derivative at a Point"}]}
